    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Regional climate modeling",
    "problem": "Coarse spatial resolution in previous European climate projection ensembles limits their usefulness for regional to local-scale impact assessments and the accurate representation of regional details, such as high-intensity precipitation, which the new high-resolution EURO-CORDEX dataset aims to address.",
    "method": "This paper presents a new high-resolution (12.5 km) regional climate simulation ensemble for Europe, based on RCP4.5 and RCP8.5 scenarios, and compares it with previous projections to provide an improved dataset for climate impact research and adaptation studies.",
    "task": "The task is to present a new high-resolution EURO-CORDEX climate change projection ensemble for Europe, analyzing its results for temperature, precipitation, and impact indices and comparing them with projections from the previous ENSEMBLES project.",
